{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause (read-only journal evidence, host i-00880b2c7f13527c5). Times are 2026-10-29 UTC; PDT is 7 hours earlier.\n- 00:40:19 and 00:46:19: rebar-health logs container rebar-mcp-e2ed08b343a2-8092 at memory_rss 3.31 GB and 3.37 GB.\n- 00:47:26: kernel `Memory cgroup out of memory: Killed process 1648385 (rebar-mcp)`. The cgroup is the container's docker scope (limit 3801088 kB). dockerd records the task delete at 00:47:27.\n- 00:47:28: the workspace index was written (its mtime). HEAD stayed at 3835269d792 while the index and working tree became e2ed08b343a, the commit that container was deployed for.\nThe container's background refresh (`git merge --ff-only origin/main` inside refresh_code_locked) was killed between writing the checkout and moving the ref, during an OOM of the same container. Every later start then saw a \"dirty\" tree and refused, with only a stderr line.\nFix in progress: (1) the entrypoint recovers exactly that provable state: index tree == a commit on HEAD..origin/main, no unstaged or untracked change, compare-and-swap ref move. Otherwise it refuses and emits an `MCP_CODE_WORKSPACE_ERROR {...}` marker. (2) The autodeploy steady-state tick checks the live backend's workspace and emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-code-workspace-stuck, which the existing rebar-autodeploy-errors alarm pages on. No config key, env var or Terraform change."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794424730523381767,"uuid":"a8bdd37b-ad17-47dc-91de-116c5a247752"}